diff --git a/diag/README.md b/diag/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..04ef51750e90
--- /dev/null
+++ b/diag/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# hawaii-diag - Moto E32 (XT2227-1, Unisoc T606) 4.14.199 kernel
+
+Branch cut from the vendor OSS drop `R-11-release-RORS` @ `c4e610cd833c`
+("Add design file") so that every local change lives in git instead of only in
+the working tree.
+
+Nothing on this branch is meant to ship.  It contains:
+
+* build fixes needed to compile the OSS drop with clang 11 / ld.lld,
+* the backports the RORS userspace expects (file refs, anon_vma counters,
+  SIPC shared-memory copies, SPRD uapi ABI),
+* **DIAG only** boot instrumentation: entry-stub hooks, framebuffer text
+  console, point-in-time probes, AON watchdog arming, late KVM init.
+
+## Where the real documentation is
+
+The PC repository is the source of truth:
+
+    C:\Users\Creitin\moto-root-test
+      docs/evidence/2026-10-30-custom-kernel-hang.txt   boot-hang investigation
+      docs/evidence/2026-10-30-boot_b-tests.txt        every flash + verdict
+      scripts/host/                                    generators, packing, flashing
+      patches/kernel-sprd/                             patch series for this branch
+
+## Commits
+
+    1  gitignore: ignore local build outputs and boot-experiment artefacts
+    2  sprd: build fixes for the OSS drop (devfreq/sfp include path, vhost ioctl)
+    3  mm/fs: backport fget_many/fput_many and split anon_vma counters
+    4  sipc: copy_from_user() variant that does not zero a shared-memory tail
+    5  uapi: SPRD jpg/vsp map sizes and sensor private-key ioctl (RORS ABI)
+    6  diag: on-panel boot tracing (paint bands, milestone line, printk mirror)
+    7  diag: generated instrumentation header snapshot (screen build, 24 bpp)
+
+The `diag/` code in commit 6 is inert unless a `DIAG_*` macro is set, except the
+`head.S` probes, which are unconditional in this branch - they write to the
+bootloader framebuffer at `0x9e000000` and cost ~nothing.
+
+## Rebuilding
+
+    cd ~/kernel-sprd
+    ./stage_build.sh <panic> <arm> <smc> <paint> <screen>
+
+    panic   0..8   panic() at that stage (only resets from stage 8 onwards)
+    arm     0..8|9 arm the AON watchdog there (9 = every stage >= 2)
+    smc     0..8   PSCI SYSTEM_RESET at that stage
+    paint   0..2   1 = one band per start_kernel() stage, 2 = setup_arch() probes
+    screen  0|1    framebuffer text console (printk mirror + milestone line)
+
+Output: `Image.p<panic>a<arm>s<smc>q<paint>c<screen>` in the tree root, plus
+`include/linux/diag_stage.h` and `include/linux/diag_font.h` generated by
+`~/prepare_stage_panics.py`.
+
+Toolchain: `~/toolchains/clang+llvm-11.0.1-x86_64-linux-gnu-ubuntu-20.10/bin`
+(the script exports it).  `.config.diagwdt` is the working config; KCFLAGS
+carries the `DIAG_*` defines for `.c` files.  **KCFLAGS does not reach `.S`
+files**, so the `head.S` probes are unconditional.
+
+## State at 2026-11-01
+
+The KVM/vhost build reaches the end of `setup_arch()` and hangs afterwards,
+before the first driver printk.  The on-panel milestone line reads
+
+    15 16 17 18 19
+
+i.e. `paging_init` ... `smp_build_mpidr_hash` all completed, and the kernel
+dies in the silent window after `setup_arch()` returns.  Stock 4.14.199 boots
+fine on the same device, so this is specific to the local change set.
+
+## Artefacts kept outside git (too large / build output)
+
+    ~/kernel-diag/images/    Image.*, System.map.*, overlay .dtbo
+    ~/kernel-diag/patches/   format-patch series + full diff of this branch
+    ~/kernel-diag/scripts/   copies of the helper scripts from $HOME
+    ~/kernel-diag/configs/   phone.config (vendor config read off the device)
